{"title":"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Point\" title=\"Point\">point</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is chosen in the interior of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> such that when <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Line\" title=\"Line\">lines</a> are drawn through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parallel\" title=\"Parallel\">parallel</a> to the sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, the resulting smaller <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangles</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab09eb0e14820db6dabcda6e9cc8638044351ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/2/5c2ba5789eea835bf50c7be61de92a6c2914e5b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/7/3c7dd94c9d9e4e5357bc67e6be8ebf07ffe2b9f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> in the figure, have <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Area\" title=\"Area\">areas</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c8e6bf4d57cd6f2bb0d7d43e00f0f442f53b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />, respectively. Find the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/3/293009bb673bfe7d5b163c98428082f101000e4d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(200); pathpen=black;pointpen=black; pair A=(0,0),B=(12,0),C=(4,5); D(A--B--C--cycle); D(A+(B-A)*3/4--A+(C-A)*3/4); D(B+(C-B)*5/6--B+(A-B)*5/6);D(C+(B-C)*5/12--C+(A-C)*5/12); MP(&quot;A&quot;,C,N);MP(&quot;B&quot;,A,SW);MP(&quot;C&quot;,B,SE); /* sorry mixed up points according to resources diagram. */ MP(&quot;t_3&quot;,(A+B+(B-A)*3/4+(A-B)*5/6)/2+(-1,0.8),N); MP(&quot;t_2&quot;,(B+C+(B-C)*5/12+(C-B)*5/6)/2+(-0.3,0.1),WSW); MP(&quot;t_1&quot;,(A+C+(C-A)*3/4+(A-C)*5/12)/2+(0,0.15),ESE); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"162\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the transversals that go through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, all four triangles are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Similar_triangles\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Similar triangles\">similar</a> to each other by the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/b/b0b3dbb5e0c16cabfa02f10ace626714ac385dbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AA$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> postulate. Also, note that the length of any one side of the larger triangle is equal to the sum of the sides of each of the corresponding sides on the smaller triangles. We use the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/2/db21f3981a4eb37853f76d4992321f144324966e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K = \\dfrac{ab\\sin C}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"103\" height=\"37\" /> to show that the areas are proportional (the sides are proportional and the angles are equal)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Alternatively, since the triangles are similar by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/b/b0b3dbb5e0c16cabfa02f10ace626714ac385dbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AA$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />, then the ratios between the bases and the heights of each of the three triangles would all be equal. The areas of each of the triangles are all perfect squares, so we could assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/5/cb5f9b6c1d45c2b3f2c963a7f41458e1b3654cdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{base}{height} = \\dfrac{2}{1}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"96\" height=\"41\" /> That means that the base of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab09eb0e14820db6dabcda6e9cc8638044351ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is 4, the base of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/2/5c2ba5789eea835bf50c7be61de92a6c2914e5b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is 6, and the base of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/7/3c7dd94c9d9e4e5357bc67e6be8ebf07ffe2b9f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is 14. Since the quadrilaterals underneath <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab09eb0e14820db6dabcda6e9cc8638044351ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/2/5c2ba5789eea835bf50c7be61de92a6c2914e5b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> are both parallelograms, and opposite sides of a parallelogram are congruent, the base of the large triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/6/bd648ed19bac0a2f6e22b4dfba9ca9cc3f10d61d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 + 14 + 6 = 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, the height of the entire triangle would be twelve, so therefore, the area of the large triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/812e86d24694338e13908d9ec2e52cda2b2d166d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot 24 \\cdot 12 = \\boxed{144}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"139\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The base of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f828f10cad9235a2c72c34369f5fd4a1179e579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Let the base of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/9/8b91b7245b0dd42b4f5585b97e323a8cfaa064a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, the base of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/0/a40dccc3bb61d55c03b7dafe15707eeef43885ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, and the base of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e51a3ca6ab05c0125032af6cc66844243477601d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/5/6459fde10e8901ed934e560ad6e728174ba909c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}, t_1, t_2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e51a3ca6ab05c0125032af6cc66844243477601d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> are all similar, the sections in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f828f10cad9235a2c72c34369f5fd4a1179e579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> that aren't <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/7/75717d94dbf9234c4d373518c1a86a6de2d8401c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1,t_2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e51a3ca6ab05c0125032af6cc66844243477601d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> are all parallelograms. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/e/47ec72ef485ccf643e62a3cdeb8585e0071426e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=x+z+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" />. We can relate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/7/75717d94dbf9234c4d373518c1a86a6de2d8401c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1,t_2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e51a3ca6ab05c0125032af6cc66844243477601d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> by the square root of the ratio of their areas. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/0/b407ef5d389817bbbf2cb8660a593bfbed69e12d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{9}}=\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"66\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/411026c23b687d6d0f5154d962f9b784b7cc1ba9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{49}}=\\frac{2}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"79\" height=\"45\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/a/06a0b637b840718bdd6d53822ac1cb68275d606f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{3x}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"55\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/2/992c282aeea317e5682293e032c49c0e57da539d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=\\frac{7x}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"38\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf3e49d67b537706f68d7404a0f9b421597cc910.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+\\frac{7x}{2}+\\frac{3x}{2}=6x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"147\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f828f10cad9235a2c72c34369f5fd4a1179e579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> has a base that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/9/8b91b7245b0dd42b4f5585b97e323a8cfaa064a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/d/f5defa3a7d9a5d964d61d0e3b0950337bbbf9422.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle{ABC}]=36[t_1]=36 \\cdot 4=\\boxed{144}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"265\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>-PhunsukhWangdu\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the three lines through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are parallel to the sides, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/9/8b91b7245b0dd42b4f5585b97e323a8cfaa064a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/0/a40dccc3bb61d55c03b7dafe15707eeef43885ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e51a3ca6ab05c0125032af6cc66844243477601d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f828f10cad9235a2c72c34369f5fd4a1179e579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> are similar by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/b/b0b3dbb5e0c16cabfa02f10ace626714ac385dbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AA$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> similarity. Suppose the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f828f10cad9235a2c72c34369f5fd4a1179e579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />, so the ratio of the base of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/9/8b91b7245b0dd42b4f5585b97e323a8cfaa064a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> to the base of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/0/a40dccc3bb61d55c03b7dafe15707eeef43885ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" /> to the base of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e51a3ca6ab05c0125032af6cc66844243477601d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> to the base of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f828f10cad9235a2c72c34369f5fd4a1179e579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/a/e9aba757acb66d08a3cb61b941759cc849b531c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2:3:7:x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />. Because the quadrilaterals below <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/9/8b91b7245b0dd42b4f5585b97e323a8cfaa064a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/0/a40dccc3bb61d55c03b7dafe15707eeef43885ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" /> are parallelograms, the base of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f828f10cad9235a2c72c34369f5fd4a1179e579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is equal to the sum of the bases of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/b/65b1f57a9915d1b8b43198e30bb72531b7dea6a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_1, t_2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/1/e51a3ca6ab05c0125032af6cc66844243477601d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/0/9b045759e9e3f06bc83fd52d16b71df8c6981a1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+3+7=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"113\" height=\"14\" /> so the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f828f10cad9235a2c72c34369f5fd4a1179e579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/a/6ba7b3141dcb61212e93c54782cec336836b828a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2=12^2=\\boxed{144}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"137\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>-Yiyj1\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the longest leg of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5bb9122bec420c090e2dd6b896d81deb722254d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, and the other leg be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/2/db29945c8bcfdcad4cc46b3e466ec1b1a0d215cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{98}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />; we see that all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triangles are similar, and we take the square root of their area ratios to find that the side ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5bb9122bec420c090e2dd6b896d81deb722254d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/b/60b64f49314817a2f327f525ae4c2f83afd819bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/f/e1f2bce73877ab24e4abe8ae41191c7620c66c1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> and the ratio of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5bb9122bec420c090e2dd6b896d81deb722254d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/4/44453b97ffe55c2d55758780096dcd87ba34c63a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/8/ea8d30f111d2f213c3486ec29afd22094d711beb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>We see that the two legs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/b/60b64f49314817a2f327f525ae4c2f83afd819bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" /> will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/1/931b7b7fc68f1f8bc72f733cb1b2796015a7a21e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3x}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"25\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/1/8619457ad79b6c7672e353deb9da5d6b74963905.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{42}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />, the two legs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/4/44453b97ffe55c2d55758780096dcd87ba34c63a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50daf67ce73825d57109088708a0426b3b84c485.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2x}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"25\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/0/72086906f7b5b061e4569810236f7793e9bab834.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{28}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />. The rectangle above these two triangles will have an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50daf67ce73825d57109088708a0426b3b84c485.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2x}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"25\" height=\"38\" /> times  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/1/8619457ad79b6c7672e353deb9da5d6b74963905.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{42}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. We can now create two rectangles, each with a base being one leg of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5bb9122bec420c090e2dd6b896d81deb722254d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and one with a height of the longer leg of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/4/44453b97ffe55c2d55758780096dcd87ba34c63a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />, and the other with a height of the shorter leg of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/b/60b64f49314817a2f327f525ae4c2f83afd819bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" />. To create these rectangles, we get rid of 2 triangles from the bottom left and right of the figure. We assume these triangles are congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/b/60b64f49314817a2f327f525ae4c2f83afd819bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/4/44453b97ffe55c2d55758780096dcd87ba34c63a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />, respectively.\n</p><p>The area of rectangle one, with a height of the longest leg of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/4/44453b97ffe55c2d55758780096dcd87ba34c63a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> and a base of the shortest leg of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5bb9122bec420c090e2dd6b896d81deb722254d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/2/db29945c8bcfdcad4cc46b3e466ec1b1a0d215cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{98}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> times <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50daf67ce73825d57109088708a0426b3b84c485.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2x}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"25\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>The area of the second rectangle will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> times <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/1/8619457ad79b6c7672e353deb9da5d6b74963905.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{42}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0d6c36fdad9c2874053be46c7e4120f2edcf47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />. The remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triangles will have a combined area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> as they are identical to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/4/44453b97ffe55c2d55758780096dcd87ba34c63a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/b/60b64f49314817a2f327f525ae4c2f83afd819bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" />. We now sum the areas of the top rectangle, our <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> rectangles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5bb9122bec420c090e2dd6b896d81deb722254d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and the bottom <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> triangles.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/e/83e2eca28ff18977660bb9cbe357f6d86f63b440.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12+28+42+49+13=\\boxed{144}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"244\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~jamespudi\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/hDsoyvFWYxc?t=199\">https://youtu.be/hDsoyvFWYxc?t=199</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME\" title=\"1984 AIME\">1984 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1984 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1984\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017174629\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.046 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.058 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 643/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1431/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 88/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 19759/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.565      1 Template:AIME_box\n100.00%    7.565      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2775:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017174629 and revision id 291336. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}